  "name": "Example: Differentiating Expressions Involving the Cotangent Function",
  "problem": "Find $\\dfrac {\\textrm d y} {\\textrm d x}$ if $y = 2x - 3\\cot x.$",
  "worked_solution": "We take the derivative of each term and then add them, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x-3cot\u2061x) \\\\  & =2-3(-{csc}^{2}\u2061x) \\\\  & =2+3{csc}^{2}\u2061x\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
